  "notes": [
   "This sheet has no characteristic (density versus exposure) curves: only spectral dye density and spectral sensitivity, so there is no 'curves' plot. Page 5 'Calibration data' lists printer target Dmax values of 2.00 / 2.00 / 1.95 (R / G / B) for several printer makes and says the recommended Dmax values are reached only with high activity chemistry (Fujifilm CPRA Digital Pro AC / ADM); that is a printer setting, not a measured curve.",
   "Both plots are raster images (blurred, dotted grid, colour-coded curves), traced by curve colour (yellow, magenta, cyan; blue, green, red).",
   "Spectral dye density (section 12, 'Process: CP48S'): y axis is 'Spectral reflection density', normalised so each dye peaks at 1.0 (axis 0, 0.5, 1; the yellow curve peaks at about 445 nm, magenta at 550 nm, cyan at about 650 nm); x axis 400-750 nm. The sheet draws no D-min or neutral curve. The yellow curve is drawn under the magenta one beyond about 665 nm (both below 0.03) and is not traced beyond that. Cyan and magenta start at about 0.34 and 0.36 at 400 nm.",
   "Spectral sensitivity (section 13): the y axis is 'Relative sensitivity' on a LINEAR scale (0, 0.5, 1), not log, normalised so that 1 is a gridline value, not each curve's peak (blue peaks at about 1.2 near 487 nm, green about 1.08 near 550 nm, red about 0.61 near 695 nm); values are recorded as printed. Footnote: sensitivity equals the reciprocal of the exposure (J/cm2) required to produce a specified density; legend: Densitometry Status A, density 1.0 above Dmin. r = red-sensitive layer (cyan-forming), g = green-sensitive (magenta-forming), b = blue-sensitive (yellow-forming). Curves are drawn only over 403-518 nm (b), 428-592 nm (g) and 600-730 nm (r).",
   "The sheet says CP48S / CP49E (Fujicolor Paper Process) or RA-4 type processes; the plots name only CP48S."
  ]
